WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.210
Lock your accounts, use Wi-Fi safely, and guard your privacy.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.750
This is the video for module three: protecting your accounts, connection and privacy.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.930
Criminals do not guess passwords one by one. Programs try millions of common passwords, and lists leaked from hacked websites.

4
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.930
So a name and birth year, or the same password everywhere, is easy to break.

5
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:35.270
Instead, pick four random words that do not belong together, and join them with a number or symbol. For example, Mango, Bicycle, Rain, Okra, 7.

6
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.770
Use a different one for each important account, and let Google Password Manager remember them for you.

7
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:53.940
For example, Yetunde in Lagos used one password on four sites. A recipe website was hacked, and then Gmail warned her about a sign-in attempt from another country.

8
00:00:55.190 --> 00:01:00.800
She changed her Gmail password first, because email resets almost every other account.

9
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:08.110
At passwords dot google dot com she ran Password Checkup, and changed every password it flagged.

10
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:16.230
Then she created a passkey, so she signs in with her fingerprint. A fake website cannot trick a passkey out of you.

11
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:31.470
Two-step verification means signing in needs something you know, your password, and something you have, your phone. Start with email. Open myaccount dot google dot com, tap Security, then 2-Step Verification.

12
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:40.190
Add Google prompts, and a second method such as an authenticator app. SMS codes are better than nothing, but weaker.

13
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.980
Get your backup codes and write them on paper. Not a photo on the same phone.

14
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:56.410
In WhatsApp, open Settings, Account, Two-step verification, and create a 6-digit PIN that is not your birthday or bank PIN.

15
00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:08.620
Watch for the wrong code trick. A friend's number says, I sent you a code by mistake, please send it back. That code is your own WhatsApp code. Sending it hands over your account.

16
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:19.770
Patience in Benin City typed her Gmail password into a fake login page by mistake. But she had turned on 2-Step Verification a month earlier.

17
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:25.560
Minutes later her phone asked, is it you trying to sign in, from another country?

18
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.270
She tapped No, it's not me, and Google blocked the sign-in.

19
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:37.340
Then she changed her password. Never approve a prompt you did not ask for, just to make it go away.

20
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:48.980
Anyone can create a Wi-Fi network with a trusted name. Zainab in Kano saw two eatery networks with almost the same name. She asked the cashier which was real.

21
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:57.700
A real sign-in page asks only for a code, phone number or room number. Never your email or bank password.

22
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:10.000
Zainab used the Wi-Fi to download a course video. But to check that her client's 45,000 naira had arrived, she turned Wi-Fi off and opened her bank app on mobile data.

23
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:23.160
When she left, she chose Forget, so her phone would not join again by itself. At home, protect your own hotspot with WPA2 or WPA3 and a long password.

24
00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:35.370
Criminals use your details to build believable scams. So once a month, check these. A torch app does not need your contacts, so remove permissions an app does not need.

25
00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:44.870
Aisha in Abuja set WhatsApp groups to My contacts and silenced unknown callers. The scam group invitations and night calls stopped.

26
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:55.210
Never post ID slips or cards. A fraudster who sees your child's school uniform can pretend to be a teacher calling about an emergency.

27
00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:04.060
Privacy is not hiding. It is choosing. Ask yourself, would I be comfortable if a stranger who wanted to cheat me saw this?

28
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:14.370
To remember. Use four random words, different for each account. Turn on two-step verification, starting with email. Never share a code.

29
00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:20.670
Keep money and passwords off public Wi-Fi. And remove app permissions an app does not need.

30
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:33.700
Now practise. Change your email password, run Password Checkup, turn on two-step verification for Google and WhatsApp, forget old public networks, and tune your privacy settings.

31
00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.990
Continue with the lessons below.
